# tests/rb-raw-readers-baseline/ — the registry of suites that read
# bin/run-build.sh as the RAW driver instead of the flatten. ONE FILE PER SUITE,
# named for the suite with .txt appended, holding the sentence that says why the
# flatten will not do for it.
#
# The flatten (tests/lib/rb-all.sh, read as $RB_ALL) puts every stage module's
# body back at its call site, so a suite reading it sees the pipeline in its
# original order at every state of the BH-478 split. A suite that reads the raw
# driver instead sees a pipeline with holes in it the moment a body moves out.
# The one honest reason to read the driver is to EXECUTE it — the flatten is not
# runnable.
#
# Adding a reader: put `# reads-run-build: raw — <why>` in that suite's header
# and add its file here. Retiring one: delete both. Two PRs doing either never
# touch the same path — which is the whole point, and why this is a directory
# of one-file entries rather than a pinned list (BH-1177).
#
# AN ENTRY IS A .txt FILE, and nothing else in here is — that is why this file
# has no extension. tests/rb-modules-source-test.sh reports any entry that does
# not name a suite that really reads the driver.
